# Files under inst/ that have no business in a user's library.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE, everything under inst/ installs. That shipped
# inst/rosc/submission.md -- a self-report written for external reviewers --
# into every user's library, where it asserted 1 345 expectations, 14
# vignettes and "0 errors / 0 notes" against a package that had 2 151, 19 and
# two NOTEs. The numbers are generated now, but the document still does not
# belong in a library: it is process, not software.
#
# NOTE ON SCOPE: .Rinstignore removes files from the INSTALLED package only.
# It does not shrink the source tarball -- that is .Rbuildignore's job -- so
# nothing here helps with the CRAN 5 MB limit.
# PATHS ARE RELATIVE TO THE SOURCE ROOT, not to inst/. The first version of
# this file said `^rosc$` and `^WORDLIST$`, which match nothing: R applies
# these patterns to `inst/rosc/...`. Verified by installing to a temporary
# library and listing it, which is the only way to know.
^inst/rosc
^inst/WORDLIST$
